Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:52:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: carry the release documents to R73 - the q6_K MMVQ
 route, with its reach stated before its percentages

Identity moves to the release engine: series 586 -> 588, tip 3f574313f -> 79f11389b (source 3cd91bf2f), tag r66i-integration-2026-09-19 -> r73i-release-engine-2026-09-21, engine arifi-b10825-r66i-aadddfb9f -> arifi-b10825-r73i-3cd91bf2f. RELEASE-NOTES-r66i.md is renamed to RELEASE-NOTES-r73i.md and the story to RELEASE-STORY-r73i.md.

New story sections 5a and 5a-gates cover what R73 shipped: the q6_K q8_1 MMVQ route default ON on AMD at n=7,8, MUL_MAT only, GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_MMVQ=legacy to revert. +5% to +40% per verify column, 58/60 paired rounds across five shapes, worst round 0.9894, per-shape table sourced from the promotion record and seat-62 4ah. MUL_MAT_ID excluded on a measured wash. 1024x5120 n=8 is a tie at 1.0087 and is disclosed, not banked.

THE REACH IS STATED BEFORE THE PERCENTAGES, in all three documents. A speculative decoder verifies at width = 1 + draft depth, so n=7,8 needs a draft depth of 6 or 7 - the DFlash2 publisher recipe's depth - and at our served depth 4 (verify width 5) the route is LATENT. Zero served tokens change on this box and no throughput claim is made.

New section 6a carries chain151: R66 vs R56 at LAUNCH level, 8 launches per arm, counterbalanced, 0 invalid, every CI contains zero, quality identical. The honest end-to-end statement is that there is no served change at draft depth 4 and the gains are per-column at verify widths 5-8. The R56 and R66 narrative is left as written - it is the history of how the fork got here.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - documents only; no code path is touched. Every number carries its receipt.
